%U A399307 9691,19382,11979,7403,4576,2827,5654,3493,6986,4317,2669,5338,10676,6597,13194,8153,16306
%N A399307 The periodic cycle of 23 in the "Lucas-Collatz" function: a(0)=23; for n>0, if a(n-1) is Lucas-odd (A399306), then a(n)=2*a(n-1); if a(n-1) is Lucas-even (A399305), then a(n) is the integer whose minimal Lucas representation (A130310) results from removing the final 0 of A130310(a(n-1)).
%C A399307 This periodic cycle comprises 132 integers, including 16 integers < 100, 65 integers between 100 and 1000, 38 integers between 1000 and 10000, and 13 integers > 10000. The largest integer in this cycle is a(30) = 19382.
%C A399307 An interesting value in the cycle is a(50) = 15402 = 15127 + 199 + 76, which has the Lucas representation 100000000101000000000. This is the first of 8 consecutive Lucas-even numbers in the sequence, resulting in the much smaller Lucas-odd number a(58) = 327 = 322 + 4 + 1, or 1000000001010 in Lucas representation.
%C A399307 Other small integers which do not occur within this cycle itself, but whose orbits reach this cycle, include 52, 64, 73, 79, 82.
%H A399307 Geoffrey Caveney, <a href="/A399307/b399307.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..132</a>
%e A399307 a(1) = 46 = 2*a(0) since a(0) = 23 is Lucas-odd because removing the final 0 of A130310(23) = 1001010 does not result in a valid minimal Lucas representation of another integer.
%e A399307 a(4) = 113 since a(3) = 184 is Lucas-even and removing the final 0 of A130310(184) = 10100100100 results in A130310(113) = 1010010010.
%Y A399307 Cf. A399305, A399306, A130310, A000032, A008884, A003124.
